WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.440
Just on the way out, we were shown something really special.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.280
This is what Raman used
to carry in his overcoat pocket.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.440
It's his personal spectroscope.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.270
So whenever he saw something interesting,

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.610
a flower, a rock, whatever.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:25.140
He could look through this and see the spectrum with its colour.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.500
This is really special because Raman

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.920
is most famous for his work on
spectroscopy,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.510
and here is his personal spectroscope.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.879
The thing that he really carried around
and valued.

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:42.790
It's like Isaac Newton's telescope or
something like that.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:46.140
This is as close as one can get

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.260
to a scientist who's sadly died.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.699
Here you can see the tools that he used,

00:00:52.699 --> 00:00:57.129
not when he was doing big experiments,
but when he was relaxing.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:00:59.689
You can imagine him: 'Look! Nice flower'

00:00:59.689 --> 00:01:04.500
and then go, looks at it, so we're very privileged.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.600
This is something I hope all of you who're watching will remember.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.060
So this is the citation,

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.740
and here is, you can perhaps guess, is the medal.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.400
Wow, if I put this near the lamp.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.640
Well I wouldn't, I've never tried it.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.040
There it goes, it's whizzing around, that's fantastic, that's really good.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.630
I've never tried that, that's a first.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.090
You did sound a bit alarmed, I was like, 'Oh no, what have I done?'

